canary backstop: only treat a +0x28 load as the guard when its compare
reloads the slot the prologue saved the guard in

The stack-canary neutralization pass rewrites `ldr Xt,[Xn,#0x28]` to
`mov Xt,#0` when it believes Xn holds TPIDR_EL0. Its BACKSTOP arm (used when
the dataflow lost track of Xn) accepts any such load in a stack-protected
function that is followed by `ldr Xu,[sp,#M] ; cmp Xt,Xu ; b.cond`. A
std::map emptiness test has exactly that shape when end() is spilled:

  libstartup.so (Instagram 455.0.0.51.72), CDN cache-key init
  0x4445a0  ldr  x8,[x11,#0x28] ; 0x4445a4 str x8,[sp,#0x228]  <- prologue guard save
  0x445258  ldr  x20,[x10,#0x28]                               <- inner map begin()
  0x445270  ldr  x8,[sp,#0x70]                                 <- spilled end()
  0x445274  cmp  x20,x8 ; b.eq 0x445160

The backstop wrote `mov x20,#0` (confirmed by reading the live code at the
fault: d2800014 where the file has f9401554). The walk then dereferenced
NULL+0x50, the null-recovery masked every following fault, and the thread
(SWPool3, CacheKeyGenerator.initializeKeyGenerator) spun at 98% CPU while
the main thread waited in isInitialized: a black window on every launch with
a logged-in session (only then is the cache-key JSON parsed).

Fix: remember, per function, the frame slot where the prologue saves the
guard it read (the store that follows the dataflow-patched prologue read;
reset at each frame push and each `sub sp,sp,#N`). The backstop declines a
candidate whose compare reloads a different offset off the same base.
Declining is the safe direction: a genuine guard read left unpatched still
faults on the TPIDR magic and is answered at fault time by the shim's
canary backstop. MACAPK_CANARY_GUARD_SLOT=0 restores the previous behavior;
the knob is part of the canary-plan cache key.

Measured: across the 42 images the pass ran on in one Instagram launch it now declines exactly one
site (libstartup+0x445258); an offline audit of the 5,764 backstop sites
that remain finds every one feeding a __stack_chk_fail check or a
straight-line epilogue. Six saved data trees that hung 6/6 now open 6/6 in
InstagramMainActivity (8-10 s).

Also adds MACAPK_FAULT_DUMP=N (default off): for the first N near-null
faults the recovery is about to mask, print the register file, the live
code before pc, 0x300 bytes above sp and 0x80 bytes behind every register
that points at readable memory (read with mach_vm_read_overwrite, so it is
fault-free inside the handler). This is how the rewrite above was found;
without a debugger (SIP, no get-task-allow) it is the only snapshot.

Applies to vendor/macapk at 57c9912 (after 0005) with `patch -p1` from
vendor/macapk.

